1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,938
Pesadilla Verde: a suffocating South American jungle, a one-way river, and a squad

2
00:00:04,938 --> 00:00:07,596
of soldiers who'd rather fight than be rescued.

3
00:00:07,816 --> 00:00:09,565
Here's how the location plays.

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:14,183
Put the Huey token in the Clearing, and the two Train cards into your Action

5
00:00:14,183 --> 00:00:14,581
Tableau.

6
00:00:14,801 --> 00:00:18,526
Lay out the Soldiers card and Action cubes, then the eight Upgrade tokens:

7
00:00:18,526 --> 00:00:21,244
the two green starters unlocked, the other six locked.

8
00:00:22,067 --> 00:00:26,192
Every normal Victim is a Soldier. Unlike normal Victims, they'll follow you into the

9
00:00:26,192 --> 00:00:28,403
Killer's space, and you can order them about.

10
00:00:28,623 --> 00:00:32,441
The Archeologist and the Rebel Leader are not Soldiers, and can't be ordered.

11
00:00:33,267 --> 00:00:37,507
In the Action phase, choose a space with Soldiers, and drop an Action cube on the

12
00:00:37,507 --> 00:00:40,648
leftmost slot of a free Action Upgrade, like Move or Attack.

13
00:00:40,868 --> 00:00:42,617
Every Soldier there carries it out.

14
00:00:42,837 --> 00:00:47,326
In Upkeep, cubes slide one slot right. Once a cube falls off, that action is free

15
00:00:47,326 --> 00:00:47,659
again.

16
00:00:48,467 --> 00:00:51,645
Your squad starts out green. Saving one costs two Time.

17
00:00:51,865 --> 00:00:55,812
When they attack, roll for each Soldier: a one or two means one of them gets shot.

18
00:00:56,032 --> 00:01:00,099
They can only hit their own space, and damage is the number of Soldiers halved,

19
00:01:00,099 --> 00:01:02,261
rounded down. A lone Soldier does nothing.

20
00:01:03,067 --> 00:01:07,773
Use the Train card to unlock Upgrades: free rescues, no friendly fire, attacks into

21
00:01:07,773 --> 00:01:11,515
adjacent spaces, and damage rounded up, so even one Soldier hurts.

22
00:01:11,735 --> 00:01:13,399
Some effects can lock them again.

23
00:01:14,233 --> 00:01:16,976
While the Huey is in the Clearing, it's an escape space.

24
00:01:16,976 --> 00:01:19,865
Stand there and you can save any number of Victims at once.

25
00:01:20,085 --> 00:01:22,005
Then the Huey leaves, so pick your moment.

26
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:25,328
The river runs one way, from the Waterfall down.

27
00:01:25,328 --> 00:01:29,485
Moving downriver, one space of movement takes you or your Soldiers as far as you

28
00:01:29,485 --> 00:01:29,745
like.

29
00:01:29,965 --> 00:01:32,995
But you pass through every space on the way, piranhas included.

30
00:01:33,215 --> 00:01:36,393
Enemies only drift one space, and no one moves upriver.

31
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:41,104
A few tips. Unlock No Friendly Fire early, or your squad thins itself out.

32
00:01:41,324 --> 00:01:45,570
Keep Soldiers together: damage is half the group, so one big squad hits far harder

33
00:01:45,570 --> 00:01:46,657
than scattered pairs.

34
00:01:46,877 --> 00:01:49,437
Gather Victims in the Clearing before you use the Huey.

35
00:01:49,657 --> 00:01:53,583
And finish anything upriver first. The river's a fast lane with no way back.

